Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 09:25:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] W3 update: block layout

WEBVIEW_PLAN.md phase W3:
- wv_layout.{h,c}: DOM -> display list (WV_D_BOX + WV_D_TEXT); block
  boxes honouring width/margin/padding; inline flow with HTML whitespace
  collapsing + word wrap; <br>; <pre>; inline style stack (b/strong
  bold, a blue+underline, u underline) nesting-safe; img 16x16
  placeholder; hr; canvas width/height block; hidden elements produce
  no boxes
- iterative by design: (node,phase) walk stack + block/inline stacks in
  caller arrays -- no recursion, nothing big on the 64 KiB stack
- UA stylesheet until W5 CSS: body 8px margin, p margins, h1-h6 bold,
  ul/ol 32px indent, blockquote margins, hr rule
- host gate: test_wv_layout.c 79 checks: wrap at viewport edge, nested
  blocks at summed margin/padding offsets, exact expected display list,
  whitespace, pre/br, hidden, styles, placeholders, 5000 boxes in
  1064 us (budget 7500 us), 1000 fuzz iterations
- QEMU gate: 5000-box doc laid out in-guest on the real 64 KiB stack
  (layout smoke: PASS, 10101 us under TCG = 10x host, not a blow-up);
  test_webview.sh asserts it (11 checks)
- bug caught: br/img missing from inline list -> <br> opened an empty
  block and never broke the line; fixed with regressions
- webview.elf ~175 KB; make test-unit green
